    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1081">

                <pb facs="0916" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3685.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-22T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 22, 1912—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. de la Barra to-day indicated in conversation the opinion that the present
                    Government could not continue to exist, though personally he hoped it might. I
                    advised him to use the utmost diligence in supporting the present Government to
                    the point where it was apparent it could not live and then to use his influence
                    with Congress.</p>
                <p>Conditions in Morelos, Guerrero, Sinaloa, and Puebla growing worse. Bodies of
                    revolutionists of from 100 to 300 in different groups have practically
                    surrounded Mexico City.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
